ID: D-19
TARGET: main
FILE: .gitattributes
OP: create
VERIFY: grep -qF '*.sh text eol=lf' .gitattributes
COMMIT: chore(gitattributes): 给 shell 脚本与步骤定义钉死 LF 行尾
---BEGIN---
# Shell scripts and step definitions must stay LF.
#
# The nightly job runs on a Linux host, where a CRLF script dies with
# `$'\r': command not found` before it does anything at all. This repository
# had no .gitattributes and the development machine has core.autocrlf=true,
# so nothing else guaranteed it — the committed blobs happened to be LF only
# because they were authored that way.
#
# These two patterns are the only ones that get a rule. In particular the
# Markdown boards keep their existing (autocrlf-driven) convention: the
# executor's normalize_body aligns each step body to whatever its target file
# actually uses, so a mixed repository still works.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.step text eol=lf
---END---
